     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 15,
     "notable_quote": "If he be Mr. Hyde, … I shall be Mr. Seek."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "location_text": "the entry of the court and the by-street of shops",
   "characters": [
    {
     "name_text": "Mr. Utterson",
     "presence": "present",
     "role": "agent",
     "para_first": 16
    },
    {
     "name_text": "Mr. Hyde",
     "presence": "present",
     "role": "agent",
     "para_first": 17
    }
   ],
   "dialogue": [
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 18,
     "notable_quote": "Mr. Hyde, I think?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 19,
     "notable_quote": "That is my name. What do you want?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 20,
     "notable_quote": "I see you are going in. I am an old friend of Dr. Jekyll’s—Mr. Utterson of Gaunt Street—you must have heard of my name; and meeting you so conveniently, I thought you might admit me."
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 21,
     "notable_quote": "You will not find Dr. Jekyll; he is from home … How did you know me?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 22,
     "notable_quote": "On your side, … will you do me a favour?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 23,
     "notable_quote": "With pleasure, … What shall it be?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 24,
     "notable_quote": "Will you let me see your face?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 25,
     "notable_quote": "Now I shall know you again. It may be useful."
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 26,
     "notable_quote": "Yes, … it is as well we have met; and à propos, you should have my address."
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 28,
     "notable_quote": "And now, … how did you know me?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 29,
     "notable_quote": "By description."
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "implicit",
     "para": 30,
     "notable_quote": "Whose description?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 31,
     "notable_quote": "We have common friends, …"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 32,
     "notable_quote": "Common friends, … Who are they?"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 33,
     "notable_quote": "Jekyll, for instance, …"
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Hyde",
     "addressee_text": "Utterson",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 34,
     "notable_quote": "He never told you. I did not think you would have lied."
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": "Hyde",
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 35,
     "notable_quote": "Come, … that is not fitting language."
    },
    {
     "speaker_text": "Utterson",
     "addressee_text": null,
     "attribution": "anaphoric",
     "para": 37,
     "notable_quote": "There must be something else. There is something more, if I could find a name for it. God bless me, the man seems hardly human!"
    }
   ]
  },
